        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization> ;
    ns5:modTime "2011-08-30T14:41:27"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ns1:hasSuccessorOrganization <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n130713> ;
    ns1:overview """<p>The Nuclear and Radiological Department was established in 1957 to contribute to research and education for peaceful uses of the atom. The Nuclear Engineering and Science has become a mature engineering discipline with various applications including homeland security, power generation, medical diagnosis&nbsp;&amp; therapy, industrial&nbsp;&amp; medical imaging, nondestructive imaging and detection, food irradiation, isotope production, and propulsion.</p>\r
<p>The mission of the Nuclear and Radiological Department is to foster and provide world-class radiological education, research and service so as to enhance the economic and social well-being of the citizens of Florida, the nation and the world.</p>\r
<p>The goal is to educate nuclear and radiological engineering professionals in areas related to the control and safe utilization of nuclear energy, radiation and radioactivity to benefit society.</p>\r
<p>&nbsp;</p>""" .

