    ns1:overview "Dr. Wagenaar is a social epidemiologist with expertise in evaluation of public policy changes and community-level interventions, using both randomized trial and time-series research designs and statistical methods. He has served on the Governing Council of the American Public Health Association and the Board of Directors of the Society for Prevention Research, and currently serves on the Science Advisory Board for Mothers Against Drunk Driving.<br />" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "wagenaar@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 327-8716" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Wagenaar's research focuses on three broad areas:group-randomized or controlled time-series trials of preventive interventions at the state, community and institutional levels designed to improve the health of children and adolescents, empirical evaluations of the effects of national, state and local public health policies; and meta-analyses of the literature on these topics. Particular content foci include alcohol use, automobile crashes, injuries and violence." .

