<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n25071> a ns2:UFCurrentEntity,
        ns2:UFEntity,
        ns1:NonAcademic,
        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person> ;
    ns5:modTime "2011-07-27T13:54:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ns1:hasTeacherRole <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1000846474>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1716091840> ;
    ns1:overview """<p>Over 30 years direct clinical / administrative experience in Research Project Management. Particular interests in medical informatics and dissemination of knowledge for regulatory support. As Project Manager, I administered a novel electronic system for complete on-line study management pioneering web-enabled IRB applications presented at the 8th International Congress on Nursing Informatics. As an experienced Research Subject Advocate, I led a team in developing a Web-Collaboration Portal as an innovative approach to managing DSMBs in a complex research enterprise. Two areas of focus are safety data integration and signal management. One goal is to develop real-time automated responses to pertinent "safety signals" to support safety-vigilance by leveraging Clinical Research Informatics for Adverse Events Reporting Systems (AERS). Background includes experience as Research Programs Coordinator, Coordinator Clinical Programs, Assistant Director Clinical Research, Research Consultant, Utilization Review, Pediatrics, Critical Care, Emergency Medicine, Physical Rehabilitation, Cardiology, Oncology, Information Communications. Worked in settings ranging through industry, academic sectors, and Veterans Affairs Research Service.Worked on NIH funded, Industry Sponsored, VA Cooperative studies. Conducted, managed or consulted on hundreds of protocols, from international multi-center trials to investigator-initiated studies, and from Phase 1 through 4, including Genetics and Pharmacogenetics. Adept interpersonal communication skills and broad command of scientific, medical and clinical concepts facilitates critical peer management components of Clinical Research Collaborations. By virtue of dedication to providing support I have continually demonstrated a facility in coordination with other research organizations, personnel, and colleagues to ensure human subjects' protections.</p>\r
Specialties\r
<p>Registered Nurse; Association of Clinical Research Professionals Certification Clinical Research Coordinator; Manuscript reviewer American Journal of Nursing; Degree Technical Communication in Health Science and Public Relations, graduate studies Public Health/ Health Communication; Graduate academic focus Health Care Marketing/ Management, Health Education, Nursing, Psychology, Project Management, Research Administration, Nursing Research, Nursing Informatics, Drug Development, Informatics.</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "kolbhr@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-8882" .

