    ns5:modTime "2011-06-16T14:18:16"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ns1:educationalTraining <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n77997> ;
    ns1:hasTeacherRole <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1128839765>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1900833714> ;
    ns1:overview "Before coming to Tacachale in 1997 Karen&rsquo;s practice focused on adult        neurological rehabilitation in both the acute and sub-acute setting. Her        specific clinic interests have been stroke and traumatic brain injury rehabilitation.        She completed the NDTA three week course in the treatment of adult hemiplegia        in 1994. <br /> While working at Tacachale her client&rsquo;s have been largely the ambulatory        but aging population and the atypical behavior/autism population. Because        she has a thirteen year old son with Asperger&rsquo;s Syndrome she brings        unique insight into the trials, tribulations, gifts, and joys that Autism        brings to life." .

