    ns1:affiliatedOrganization <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n765323>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n8237463> ;
    ns1:overview """<p>Established in 1910, the&nbsp;Electrical and Computer Engineering&nbsp;department has built an international reputation for excellence in teaching, research, and service.&nbsp; As a major engineering department,&nbsp;they have an enrollment of approximately 750 undergraduate and 500 graduate students pursuing degrees in electrical and computer engineering.</p>\r
<p>Their graduate program is consistently ranked among the best in the country and with high quality students and outstanding faculty; the department is well poised to achieve its mission of excellence which reads as follows:</p>\r
<p>The mission of the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering is to offer undergraduate and graduate degree programs in electrical and computer engineering and to conduct research which serves the needs of Florida and the nation.</p>""" ;
    ns1:subOrganizationWithin <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1278118> .

