        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1607818946>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1724126200>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n620579401> ;
    ns1:overview "Robert R. Carroll, M.D., is a University of Florida  physician board  certified in Internal Medicine, Hematology, and Medical  Oncology who  has experience in the clinical treatment of breast cancer.&nbsp; For the past  nine years, before returning to  the University, he ran a private  practice devoted exclusively to the medical oncology  aspects of breast  cancer.&nbsp; This practice  included an extensive clinical trials effort,  genetic testing for abnormalities  of BrCa1 and BrCa2, management of  chemotherapy and hormonal treatments, and  guidance and recommendations  for breast cancer prevention in women who were at  high risk for  developing the disease." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "carrorr@medicine.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-7832" .

