        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n961385019> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Jen Day Shaw is the Assistant Vice President/Dean of Students for Student Affairs. The Assistant Vice President and Dean of Students' responsibilities include oversight of Student Conduct and Conflict Resolution, Disability Resource Center, New Student Programs (which includes Preview, First Year Florida, the Common Reader program and Convocation), as well as managing the 24-hour Crisis/Emergency duty for the campus and serving as chair of the Behavioral Consultation Team. She serves as the Division of Student Affairs' liaison to Academic Affairs to ensure a seamless learning experience for students. She is available to consult with faculty and staff regarding student behavior and with the university over large-scale student events." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jends@dso.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-1261 ext. 211" .

