    ns1:educationalTraining <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n232564>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n243369>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n78595> ;
    ns1:hasTeacherRole <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1302108884>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1303635417>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1348943196>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1395145113>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1859671>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n497998201> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Shaw is an expert in surgical removal of cancers, focusing on cancers of the head and neck, skin and connective tissue, and breast. With two years of additional training dedicated to the complex care of the cancer patient, she is well versed in the latest surgery and treatment options. Her expertise includes surgical solutions for cancers of the adrenal, thyroid and parathyroid glands, as well as sarcomas, melanomas, and breast cancer. She offers sensitivity, compassion and a high level of care to her patients, and welcomes the challenge to provide cures from the most complex cases." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "christiana.shaw@surgery.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 265-0535" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "With a master&rsquo;s degree in clinical research from Drexel University, Dr. Shaw also operates ongoing studies on how obesity affects patients with cancer." .

