    ns1:outreachOverview """Research/Extension Programs:<br />\r
<ul>\r
<li>Rootstock evaluation for root‐knot nematode resistance to Meloidogyne floridensis in peach production systems</li>\r
</ul>\r
<ul>\r
<li>Optimization of fertilizer management programs for stone fruit in sub‐tropical climates</li>\r
</ul>\r
<ul>\r
<li>Transfer of numerous technologies from research teams to growers via applied research projects to improve production efficiency leading to more sustainable practices</li>\r
</ul>\r
<ul>\r
<li>Educational efforts for growers leading to sustainable production practices via numerous publications, field days, workshops and short courses</li>\r
</ul>""" ;
    ns1:overview "Mercy Olmstead is the Statewide Extension Specialist for Stone Fruit Production.&nbsp; She is responsible for  		maintaining an active research program in optimizing stone fruit production practices, including crop load management,  		efficient production practices and nutrition management.&nbsp; She works with various UF/IFAS stations around the state  		and with several multi county extension agents to address establishment and production issues in stone fruit.<br /><br /> She is also responsible for effective communication transfer of research results and improvements in stone fruit production  		with the goal of expanding a competitive stone fruit industry in Florida.&nbsp; She authors and maintains the Stone Fruit Website (http://hos.ufl.edu/stonefruit)." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "mercy1@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-4772" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Ecosystem management and integration of sustainable production practices to<br />improve economic efficiency of perennial fruit crops." .

