        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n2138170740> ;
    ns1:overview "I have a doctorate in educational psychology from the State University of New York at Buffalo, a master&rsquo;s degree in measurement and statistics from SUNY Buffalo and a bachelor&rsquo;s degree in speech and drama from Syracuse University. Between degrees, I taught high school English for four years in New York state." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "cemihovich@coe.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-4472" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My major research interests include children&rsquo;s language use; literacy issues; race, class and gender equity issues; school-university partnerships; and teacher education. I have extensive experience as an evaluation consultant with organizations such as the Getty Foundation, the Educational Testing Service, state and federal agencies, and public school districts." .

