    ns1:overview "Dr. Reboussin heads the Libraries' African Studies collections in support of academic research and teaching programs relating to the African continent across all disciplines in the sixteen colleges at UF. He is an anthropologist and librarian with field experience in West Africa, and is a faculty affiliate of the Center for African Studies, one of twelve US Title VI National Resource Centers for African Area Studies. He is a faculty member appointed in the George A. Smathers Libraries' Special &amp; Area Studies Collections Department." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "danrebo@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-2642" .

