    ns1:hasTeacherRole <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1296611613>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1360572239>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n454362148>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n78823254> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Yehia Daaka is one of the leading prostrate cancer scientists in the world. He is a specialist in cell biology and pharmacology. Dr. Daaka's extensive research on the function of G protein-coupled receptors has contributed to their recognition as targets for cancer therapy, and over the last decade, several anti-cancer drugs have been developed against these molecules as a result. His research and training is supported by grants from the National Institutes of Health and the Department of Defense as well as private and nonprofit foundations. He currently holds more than &nbsp;$1 million in grants and has served as a grants reviewer for 10 years. In addition to his notable research, Dr. Daaka is an accomplished educator and mentor. He teaches courses focused on urological oncology, cancer research and cell biology. He has an extensive history of mentoring undergrads and high school students, in addition to graduate/medical students, postdoctoral fellows and junior faculty." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "ydaaka@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-8112" .

