        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n281882623> ;
    ns1:overview "In 2003 I left the National Cancer Institute to become Chief of the Geriatrics Branch at the National Institute on Aging. As my Residency and Fellowship training occurred at an institution with one of the first HCFA-supported demonstration projects in Cancer Rehabilitation and my clinical practice comprised predominantly older cancer patients with multiple morbidities, the transition from Hematology and Oncology to Geriatrics was a natural evolution, and I recently left NIA to pursue clinical geriatrics research at the Institute on Aging at the University of Florida.<br />" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "snayfield@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 265-7227" .

