    ns1:overview "Dr. Staras is an infectious disease epidemiologist with a concentration in prevention of sexually transmitted diseases and congenital infections. Her research interests include HIV, HPV, and other sexually transmitted infections. Dr. Staras is interested in the role of event level alcohol use and partner selection in acquisition of HIV and other sexually transmitted diseases. She is also currently studying adolescent, parent, and provider factors associated with receipt of the HPV vaccine among low-income adolescent girls." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "sstaras@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 265-2553" .

