    ns1:overview "Amy Zerba teaches online journalism, multimedia storytelling and visual journalism. She spent 10 years as a journalist, working as a copy editor / page designer at the Sun-Sentinel, Houston Chronicle and Austin American-Statesman and most recently as a multimedia producer at CNN.com. She is an Alligator editor alum as well." ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(512) 699-2347" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Her area of research focuses on young adults (ages 18-29) and their news habits and non-news habits -- from print newspapers to online to social media. Two of her most recent projects include: examining the reasons behind why some young adults don't read print news; and experimenting with ways to increase relevancy, comprehension, interest and informativeness of news stories for a young adult audience." .

