<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n765314> a ns2:UFEntity,
        ns1:College,
        ns8:Thing,
        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent>,
        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization> ;
    ns5:modTime "2011-04-13T23:28:07"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ns1:overview """<p>The College of Design, Construction and Planning (DCP) at the University of Florida was&nbsp; established in 1925, the college has become one of the largest design, planning and construction institutions in the country with more than 1,500 students.</p>\r
<p>DCP is home to five independent professional disciplines: architecture, building construction, interior design, landscape architecture and urban and regional planning.&nbsp; The college also is home to an interdisciplinary program in historic preservation, which allows graduate students to gain expertise in research and application of historic preservation in the United States and abroad.</p>""" ;
    ns1:subOrganizationWithin <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n765319> .

