        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n995415373> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Linda Childers Hon is executive associate dean of the College, a professor in the Department of Public Relations and the Al and Effie Flanagan Professor of Journalism and Communications at the University of Florida. Hon also held the title of University of Florida Research Foundation Professor. Hon's teaching areas include public relations theory, research methods, strategy, and campaigns. Her research focuses on public relations evaluation, relationship management, and gender and diversity issues in public relations." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "lhon@jou.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-2745" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Hon&rsquo;s research involves developing relationship theory and instrumentation vis-&agrave;-vis organizations&rsquo; major stakeholders, including customers, investors/donors, employees, government, the community, and activist publics. Measurement of relationship strategies and outcomes is a critical component of evaluating the effectiveness of public relations. The other major focus is gender issues in public relations, particularly women in the workplace." .

