        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n948852333> ;
    ns1:overview """<p>Bernard A. Mair is Associate Provost for Undergraduate  Affairs and  Professor of Mathematics at the University of Florida (UF). He has held faculty  positions at The Pennsylvania  State University and Texas Tech University before  joining the  University of Florida in 1989. Since then he has held visiting   professorships at Dartmouth College (in mathematics)and Emory University  (in  radiology).</p>\r
In 1999-2000, Dr. Mair helped to form the Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics Activity Group on Imaging Sciences (SIAGIS), and later served for two years as its secretary.&nbsp;\r
<p>Mr. Mair has served as Associate Chair and Graduate  Coordinator in the  UF mathematics department, co-director of the Center  for Applied Mathematics at  UF, and head of the mathematics department  at North Carolina State University.  From 2008-2009, Mair served as  Associate Dean in the UF College of Liberal Arts  &amp; Sciences.</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "bamair@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 846-1761" .

