    ns5:modTime "2011-06-16T15:40:37"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ns1:hasTeacherRole <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1147613943>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1157473585>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1307693972>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1592654007>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1631461641>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n2116067134>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n285588402>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n591232569>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n630992886>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n727569317>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n986810563> ;
    ns1:overview """<p>Timothy H. Leslie was graduated from the University of Florida, College        of Health Professions in 1983. Since graduating, he has worked in skilled        nursing facility, acute care, home health, and long-term care settings.        He has been a physical therapy consultant for hospice.</p>\r
<p>He has worked with adults with intellectual/developmental disabilities        since 1985 and has worked at University of Florida-Tacachale since 1986.        While there, he has worked as a staff physical therapist, Assistant Director        of Programming, and Director of Programming. He has been a clinical instructor        and has been a teaching assistant for entry level physical therapy students        in the Physical Therapy Assessment/Evaluation class at the University of        Florida.</p>\r
<p>He has been a member of the American Physical Therapy Association since        1980.</p>\r
<p>He particularly enjoys "playing" as part of his therapy sessions        with his clients and the team comradery at Tacachale, teaching students        the "art of caring" for clients, and the flexibility that working        for the University of Florida provides.</p>""" .

