        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n879158718>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n990229637> ;
    ns1:overview "<strong></strong>Dr.  Cox is teaching nurse-midwifery&nbsp;for the graduate program. She  previously taught for the Florida&nbsp;Gulf Coast University, Fort Myers,&nbsp;in  the BSN program." ;
    ns1:researchOverview """<p>Dr. Cox&rsquo;s research focuses<strong> </strong>on  the social, political, and economic aspects of midwifery and women&rsquo;s  health, including health disparities in disadvantaged and vulnerable  populations. She also has a background in medical anthropology. Her  recent research focused on decision-making for mode of delivery for  women with a previous cesarean section. She is also interested in global  women&rsquo;s health issues, such as the reduction of maternal mortality and  the training of skilled birth attendants.</p>\r
<p>Dr. Cox's  Research interests include vaginal birth after cesarean; process and  outcomes of midwifery care; social and economic determinants of health  disparities.</p>""" .

