        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n614090034>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n809518097>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n824427727> ;
    ns1:overview "Laurence B. Alexander is an Associate Dean of the UF Graduate School, Director of the Office of Graduate Minority Programs, and a Professor in the Department of Journalism. He served as Chair of the UF Department of Journalism 1994-98. In 2001, he was selected as an inaugural Provost Fellow in the UF Office of Academic Affairs.<br />Alexander chairs the Graduate Curriculum Committee and administers a dozen student development and funding programs. He leads the Graduate School&rsquo;s program in recruitment, success and graduation of underrepresented minority students. In that role, he has generated more than $7 million as a Principal or Co-Principal Investigator on federal grants and through other development efforts to support students.&nbsp;" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Research focuses on the First Amendment, freedom of expression, media law and policy issues in news gathering, and student free speech issues. He is co-author of a new book, Student Free Speech and Public Higher Education, which was published in 2010 by the Education Law Association." .

