        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n56229>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n96066> ;
    ns1:hasTeacherRole <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1159376053>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1269247034>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1300178211>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1414902830>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1448274236>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n1475652771>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n2065838651>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n226990797>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n373410835>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n43695123>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n576143310>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n603505588>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n685006516>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n697008598> ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My research interest is in the area of applied mathematics with a special emphasis on analysis and development of new numerical methods. I am interested in numerical approximation of solutions of partial differential equations, in particular finite element method. In recent years, I got interested in biological and medical applications of partial differential equations and started several collaborations in these areas. My current work related to these applications is on spatial epidemic models, magnetic resonance&nbsp; imaging (MRI), and inverse problems arising in optical tomography." .

