        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n867555823> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Andrea Gabrielli is a Diplomate of the Italian Board of General  Surgery, the American Board of Anesthesiology and holds a certificate of  special qualifications in Critical Care Medicine. He completed  Fellowships in Cardiothoracic Anesthesiology at the Cleveland Clinic  Foundation in 1992 and in Critical Care Medicine at the University of  Florida in 1993. Dr. Gabrielli is the Medical Director of the Hyperbaric  Chamber at Shands Hospital and the Medical Director of Respiratory  Therapy at the University of Florida. His clinical research interests  include critical care medicine, liver transplantation, vascular and  cardiac anesthesia, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, hyperbaric medicine  and mechanical ventilation. Dr. Gabrielli is a member of the American  Heart Association National Basic Life Support Committee and the  Educational Committee of the American Society of Critical Care  Anesthesiology." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "agabrielli@anest.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-7094" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Gabrielli's clinical research interests include critical care medicine, liver  transplantation, vascular and cardiac anesthesia, cardiopulmonary  resuscitation, hyperbaric medicine and mechanical ventilation." .

