        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n798488633> ;
    ns1:overview "Ms. Hill graduated with a Bachelor's degree in Nursing from Florida State University in 1979. She worked in Oncology and Psychiatry at Baptist Hospital in Pensacola for three years prior to entering graduate school at the University of Florida College of Nursing. She completed her Master's degree in in Psychiatric Mental Health Nursing 1984 and is licensed as an Advanced Registered Nurse Practitioner (ARNP) in Psychiatry. Ms Hill joined the Department of Psychiatry in 1984 as a Clinical Nurse Specialist and then joined the faculty as an Associate in Psychiatry in 1990. She served as the Administrative Assistant to the Child Psychiatry Divison Chief from 1985 to 1999, directed daily operations on the Children's Mental Health Unit, served as Director of the ADHD clinic, served on the Child Psychiatry Consultation-Liaison service to Pediatrics for 15 years, served as a therapist on the Adolescent Inpatient Unit, and provided clinical evaluation and treatment services in the Child And Adolescent Psychiatry Outpatient Clinic. Ms Hill has also served as the Medical student coordinator for their outpatient clinic rotation. Ms. Hill has also served as the research coordinator for two pharmaceutical-sponsored multi-center inpatient clinical trials; involving the use of Depakote in the treatment of patients with Bipolar Disorder and the treatment of memory loss in patients receiving Electro-Convulsive Therapy. She has also served on the Department of Psychiatry Institutional Site Review Committee for the Department of Children and Families, and conducted site visits at DCF facilities. In addition Ms. Hill lectures and provides clinical supervision in both the General Psychiatry Residency and Child Psychiatry Fellowship programs. She serves as a Consultant to the Center for Autism and Related Disabilities located at the University of Florida and as such, regularly consults with school districts and provides community trainings on Autism and related issues. Ms Hill also holds courtesy faculty appointment in the college of nursing as an affiliate Associate in Nursing. She serves as preceptor for Graduate students in Nursing and has lectured in their program." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "susanhill@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 265-4357" .

