    ns1:overview "Professor Kirk teaches financial reporting in the undergraduate and graduate curriculum. His research interests are the financial reporting and disclosure choices of managers and how these choices affect the quality of the information reported, the valuation of the firm, and the responses of capital market participants. He is also interested in the integral role of accounting within an economy's institutional infrastructure. His research has been published in journals such as Accounting, Organizations, and Society and Journal of Financial Economics, and presented at various invited university seminars including the University of Chicago, Northwestern and London Business School." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "marcus.kirk@cba.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-0222" .

