        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n776748230>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n907496734>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n997242145> ;
    ns1:overview "<p>Dr. Lall attended the University of Central Florida on a Valedictorian Scholarship, where she earned a B.S. degree in Biology with cum laude honors. After graduating from St. George&rsquo;s University School of Medicine in Grenada, Dr. Lall did her internship and psychiatry residency at the Medical College of Virginia (Virginia Commonwealth University). She then completed a fellowship in Child and Adolescent Psychiatry at the Johns Hopkins Hospital where she was selected to be Chief Fellow for 2004-2005. As part of her fellowship training at JHH and the affiliated Kennedy Krieger Institute, she has extensive experience in the assessment and treatment ofneurodevelopmental/autism spectrum disorders. Dr. Lall joined our faculty in 2005 and has served as the Director of the Pediatric Mood Disorders clinic. She is board certified by the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology in both General Psychiatry and in Child and Adolescent Psychiatry.</p>" .

