        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n928110715>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n977008382> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Cardenas-Lailhacar has 12 years of experience in Industrial Energy Efficiency and Management, and has done more than 220 Energy Auidts. He teaches the courses on &ldquo;Industrial Energy Management&rdquo;, and &ldquo;International Industrial Energy Management Consulting&rdquo;, at the University of Florida and energy usage optimization. His research is the various areas of energy-energy efficiency-environment-sustainability and their connection. Pollutants sequestration, energy efficiency in manufacturing processes and equipment: lighting, motors, HVAC systems, chillers, air compressors, boilers, etc. Applications and symbiotic relation of renewable and lesser known, energy sources to industry. Energy as a development indicator in undeveloped countries. Software for Energy Management, project evaluation, etc. He has implemented Industrial Energy Management Research Centers in Peru and Venezuela, and is working on others in Chile, Colombia and Ecuador." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "c.cardenas@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-1464 ext. 2009" .

