    ns1:overview """<p>My study is focused on fundamental solution of governing equations, principles of engineering analysis, calculus, and programming. I enjoy learning, reading and interacting with students, research staff, engineers in practice. I like to get associated with sharp minds who dare solving challenging engineering and physics problems.</p>\r
<p>&nbsp;</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jchun@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-9537 ext. 1512" ;
    ns1:researchOverview """<p>On-going research areas:</p>\r
<p>(1) Fundamental solution of elastic settlement in heterogeneous conditions</p>\r
<p>(2) Discrete element modeling of dynamic pile driving and static capacity determination</p>\r
<p>(3) Iron dissolution and precipitation process in solute transport in groundwater systems</p>\r
<p>(4) Finite element method and its application to shallow foundation modeling in layered soil/rock</p>\r
(5) Finite volume analysis of coupled multi-phase flow, conjugate heat transfer, and biodegradation in geochemical process""" .

