        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n966452071> ;
    ns1:overview "<p>Dr. Neiva received her D.D.S. degree at Universidade do Vale do  Itajai and completed her Certificate in Endodontics at Universidade  Federal do Parana, both in Brazil. In 2001 she joined the University of Michigan School of Dentistry  where she performed preclinical and clinical teaching and basic science  research. In 2003 Dr. Neiva joined the Oral Health Sciences Ph.D.  Program at University of Michigan and her research interests included  angiogenesis, molecular biology, and head and neck cancer. More  specifically, she explored the crosstalk between endothelial cells and  tumor cells in head and neck cancer and received her Ph.D. degree in  2009. During her training, Dr. Neiva has received numerous awards  including AADR Hatton Award, William J. Gies Award, Research Day Awards,  Rackham Block Grant Awards, Keystone Symposia Scholarship, and Dr.  Dominic Dziewiatkowski Award. Currently, she is a Post Doctoral Research Fellow in the  Departments of Periodontology and Oral Biology and an Adjunct Clinical  Assistant Professor in the Department of Endodontics.</p>" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "kneiva@dental.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-5435" .

