        <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization> ;
    ns5:modTime "2013-09-07T21:44:29"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ns1:overview """<p>The College of Agricultural and Life Sciences (CALS) administers the degree programs of the University of Florida's Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences (UF/IFAS). <a href="http://ifas.ufl.edu/">IFAS</a> is a federal, state, and local government partnership dedicated to develop knowledge in agriculture, human and natural resources, and the life sciences and to make that knowledge accessible to sustain and enhance the quality of human life.</p>\r
<p>The mission of the College of Agricultural and Life Sciences is to provide undergraduate and graduate students with a high quality education that results in knowledge and abilities for gainful employment and additional education, productive citizenship, and lifelong learning in the areas of food, agriculture, natural resources, and life sciences as they relate to human resources, the environment, individual communities, and a global society.</p>""" ;
    ns1:subOrganizationWithin <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n4777238> .

