    ns1:overview "Tom Krynski has worked in radio-TV news since 1972, and has been news director at the University of Florida since April 1985. He has seen many changes during his tenure. WRUF uses a digital newsroom computer program, which allows anchor/producers to have a \"paperless\" newscast, and eliminates reel to reel tape, as well as \"carts.\". He has been active in the Florida Associated Press Broadcasters Association, including terms as president and vice president. He also served as a state coordinator for the Radio-Television News Directors Association." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "tkrynski@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-6397" .

