    ns1:overview "Professor McGill is the Director of the Fisher School of Accounting, an Associate Dean of the Warrington College of Business Administration, and holds the PricewaterhouseCoopers endowed Professorship in Accounting. Professor McGill is a CPA (licensed in Texas) and spent several years in practice with Ernst and Whinney prior to earning his PhD. Professor McGill teaches various graduate and undergraduate tax courses, including a graduate course in international taxation, and previously served as the coordinator of the accounting PhD program." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "mcgill@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-0219" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "He is the recipient of competitive research grants from Deloitte and Touche, Ernst &amp; Young, Price Waterhouse, the AICPA, the Andrus Foundation, Fannie Mae's Housing Policy Research Division, the National Association of Realtors, and the National Homebuilder's Association." .

