        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n366813049>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n530922964>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n563563896>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n739055144>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n947630605> ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My current research interest is the luminosity calibration problem,  in particular using astrometric data (trigonometric parallaxes and proper  motions).  More particularly I have studied biases associated with  parallaxes, including the Trumpler-Weaver and Malmquist biases and the  Lutz-Kelker effect for samples as well as some newer ones.  In the past  I have considered a Bayesian approach to the problem as well as  transformation methods." .

