    ns1:primaryEmail "steven@flmnh.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-1721" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "I study the phylogenetic and phytogeographic history of various flowering plant families based based on fossil remains of flowers, fruits, pollen, leaves and wood in the range of 20 to 80 million years old. The fossils are collected mainly from Paleocene and Eocene floras of western North America, eastern Asia, and central Europe. I have documented the earliest fossil bananas, kiwi fruits, walnuts, grapes, and other familiar fruits from the early Tertiary of western North America. I enjoy the detective work that is necessary in order to reassemble extinct plant species and genera from their detached fossil organs. This work provides new taxonomic and morphological data for inclusion in phylogenetic and analyses of angiosperms.<br /><br /><br />" .

