    ns1:primaryEmail "kmin@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-2720" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My research interests are (1) constraining thermal histories of  terrestrial and meteoritic materials using (U-Th)/He and 40Ar/39Ar  thermochronometers, and (2) improving fundamentals of these methods.&nbsp;  The 40Ar/39Ar and (U-Th)/He methods play an increasingly important role  in understanding an enormous range of crustal processes, such as rate of  sedimentation, timing of volcanic eruption, timing and rate of orogenic  events, development of topography, erosional processes, and movement of  faults.&nbsp; Thermal histories of meteorites may provide key information on  the dispersion of energy and materials during the early solar system,  internal structure and heat budget of early asteroids or planets,  igneous activities and shock-induced impact metamorphism in other  planets." .

