    ns1:overview "Dr. Vertucci completed both his D.M.D. degree and specialty training in  endodontics at the University of Medicine and Dentistry of New Jersey.   He holds board certification in endodontics and is a fellow of the  American and International College of Dentists.  He joined the  Department of Endodontics at the University of Florida in 1975, was  named department chairman in 1980, and became the director of the  Postgraduate Endodontic Program in 1996.  Dr. Vertucci has received the  Teacher of the Year Award and Outstanding Clinical Professor Award in  recognition of his teaching. Dr. Vertucci retired from the University of Florida Department of  Endodontics on February 28, 2010 after 35 years of dedicated service.   Dr. Vertucci was elected Professor Emeritus status by his colleagues." ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Vertucci is currently researching the effects of new endodontic material and  effect of calcium hydroxide and endosonics on canal disinfection and  cleanliness." .

