    ns1:primaryEmail "djcant@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(904) 209-0430" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Cantliffe&rsquo;s present interests entail an enormous project related to protected production of high value vegetable crops for Florida producers.  Presently, Florida vegetable production is valued at over $1.6 billion farm gate value and is produced on almost 300,000 acres of land.  Florida vegetable culture involves intensive production practices which have caused major challenges for the vegetable industry in the State of Florida.  The Protected Ag project is looking to circumvent these challenges by developing a closed production system in passive ventilated high roof greenhouses, much of the style of which are presently being used in Israel and other middle eastern countries.  The emphasis of his work relates to sustainability for both water and fertilizer, and strives to reduce pesticides inputs to a minimum. The Protected Ag project at the University of Florida under Dr. Cantliffe&rsquo;s guidance has provided much needed information for hands on training and demonstration so that Florida producers can examine, work, and train for this exciting new agricultural business endeavor." .

