    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-4262" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Gagnon&rsquo;s research projects focus on  the study of policies and practices, as well as researched-based  instruction that promote the provision of appropriate educational  services for youth with special needs in exclusionary school settings.  He conducts research on curriculum, assessment, and accountability  policies in exclusionary school settings in light of standards-driven  reform. Specifically, he has completed national studies concerning these  topics for elementary and secondary day treatment and residential  schools (DTR) for students with emotional disturbances (ED), as well as  juvenile correctional schools. He has also completed national studies on  program characteristics and entrance and exit policies within  elementary DTR schools. Additionally, Dr. Gagnon has conducted research  and published extensively on mathematics instruction for secondary  students with ED and learning disabilities (LD)." .

