    ns1:overview "Dr. George Fitzpatrick is a professor of Environmental Horticulture  Department, at the Fort Lauderdale Research and Education Center. His  teaching includes courses in palm production and culture, arboriculture,  composting technology, and others. His research interests center on  horticultural substrates, with emphasis on the influence of process  parameters on the efficacy of compost products used as growing medium  components. In his free time, Dr. Fitzpatrick enjoys collecting and  restoring vintage early 20th century electronic devices, meteorological  instruments and timepieces." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "fitz@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(954) 577-6331" .

