        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n888389110> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Hasell specializes in the transaction between people and space focused on special populations such as women, elderly, disabled and low income people. She investigates and develops participatory action research strategies that involve people in decision making about their homes, workspaces, schools and community places. Educational facilities in higher education and K-12 are the focus of her recent work in design studios with students.<br /><br />Dr. Hasell co-authored a book titled Accessible Design Review Guide: ADAAG Compliance in Building and Site Plans and Specifications. She has published many articles and delivered numerous national and international papers aimed at developing a theoretical base and improved research within the discipline of interior design. She is a registered Interior Designer in the State of Florida.<br />" .

