    ns1:overview "Hardin is a Clinical Assistant Professor at the Medication Therapy  Management Call Center in the Department of Pharmacotherapy and  Translational Research at the University of Florida.&nbsp; She earned her  Doctor of Pharmacy degree from the University of Florida College of  Pharmacy in 2005.&nbsp; After graduation, she became a Pharmacy Manager for  Publix Pharmacy becoming one of the chain&rsquo;s first immunizing  pharmacists.&nbsp; Working with students has always been her passion; she  became a preceptor and a professor of pharmacology at City College in  Gainesville.&nbsp; Since her graduation from University of Florida, Hardin  maintained a relationship with the University through guest teaching in  Pharmacotherapy courses and in 2010 became a Clinical Assistant  Professor in the MTM Call Center providing comprehensive medication  reviews to Medicare patients.&nbsp; The center is a Geriatric and Drug  Information rotation site where Hardin helps precept twelve 4th year  pharmacy students, two residents, and one fellow." ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-9627" .

