    ns1:overview "I am interested in the physiological ecology of amphibians and reptiles, including integrative studies that incorporate morphology and behavior. I am interested in almost all aspects of the biology of snakes and tree frogs. I also have long-standing interests in conservation biology, fire ecology, and animal coloration." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "hblill@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-1101" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Adaptation of structure and function and the physiological ecology of vertebrates, especially reptiles and amphibians. The interface of physiology with ecology, behavior, morphology, andevolutionary biology." .

