    ns1:overview "Jason Rothman is an Assistant Professor of Spanish and Linguistics in the Departments of Spanish and Portuguese Studies and Linguistics at the University of Florida." ;
    ns1:researchOverview "His main research program investigates the acquisition of complex syntax and semantics pertaining to the Determiner Phrase (DP), subjunctive modality, properties of Control, pronominal objects and subjects, as well as grammatical and lexical aspect. L2/L3 acquisition, bilingual/heritage speaker acquisition of morphosyntax and semantics Other areas of interest: acquisition theory epistemology; L1 acquisition; Formal syntactic theory, diachronic change; sociolinguistics; Spanish in the US and as a world language." .

