    ns1:overview """<p>Mansour joined University of Florida, College of Pharmacy as a  clinical assistant professor at the St. Petersburg campus in October  2008. She received her Pharm.D. degree from the Lebanese American  University in 2002. Prior to completing an ASHP pharmacy practice  residency at Bayfront Medical Center in St. Petersburg, Fla., Mansour  practiced hospital pharmacy for a year. During her residency, she earned  a teaching certificate from UF while she was serving as a teaching  assistant at the St. Petersburg campus. Mansour became board-certified  in pharmacotherapy in 2007.</p>\r
<p>She worked as an adult internal medicine clinical pharmacist for  three years before joining the college of pharmacy. At UF St. Petersburg  campus, she has taught in Pharmacotherapy III and HIV elective courses  and facilitated pharmacotherapy I, communications and cases in  pharmacotherapy V. Her areas of interests are adult internal medicine  and infectious disease. She practices inpatient infectious disease  pharmacy at Baypines VA in St. Petersburg, Florida. She is also involved  in the students&rsquo; activities and serves as an advisor for the Florida  Society of Health-System Pharmacists for the St. Petersburg campus  chapter.</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "" .

