    ns1:overview "PhD, MPH, OTR/L, FAOTA is an Associate Professor in the Department of Occupational Therapy and Director of the University of Florida&rsquo;s Institute for Mobility, Activity and Participation. Dr. Classen is a nationally funded prevention-oriented scientist, who uses a public health and rehabilitation science<br />perspective to research the screening, evaluation and intervention processes for at-risk older drivers and adolescents, and those drivers with neurological conditions. Dr. Classen has 50 publications in these areas of study, seven book chapters, and is editor of three special journal issues. Dr. Classen serves on various Transportation Research Board committees, is a member of the editorial board of the Canadian Journal for Occupational Therapy, and a Fellow of both the Gerontological Society of America and the American Occupational Therapy Association. She mentors junior faculty, post-doctoral fellows, graduate and undergraduate students in Occupational Therapy, Rehabilitation Science, Public Health and Epidemiology." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "sclassen@phhp.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6062" .

