    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-1491" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Peng's overall research interest is in planning for sustainability from   the perspectives of transportation and land use planning in the context of   globalization and technological innovation. He examines how the planning   process, particularly the transportation and land use planning process, could   be improved by Information Communication Technologies to enhance sustainable   development, and how urban researchers and planners can take advantage of new   technologies to advance urban and regional planning and design. Furthermore,   he is interested in sustainable development in the developing world. His   recent research involved in the use of geospatial technologies and Web   technologies to improve urban transit planning, to enhance public participation   in community planning, to advance the sharing of distributed geospatial data based   on open geospatial standards, and to adapt to climate change. He is also   working closely with colleagues in China on urban planning and   transportation issues in the rapid economy." .

