        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n52350>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n70613> ;
    ns1:overview "The UF College of Education, founded in 1906, ranks among the top 25 public education colleges in the elite Association of American Universities. The college has three nationally ranked programs in the 2010 US News &amp; World Report survey of America&rsquo;s Best Graduate Schools: Counselor Education (No. 3), Special Education (No. 5) and Educational Administration (No. 26). The college&rsquo;s 105 distinguished faculty members engage in innovative research and public scholarship that enhance school improvement, student achievement, school readiness and leadership development in the numerous education disciplines. Nearly 1,900 students are enrolled in 21 bachelor&rsquo;s and advanced degree programs, offered within the academic areas of Teaching and Learning, Special Education and Early Childhood Studies, Counselor Education, School Psychology, Educational Administration and Higher Education, and Research and Evaluation Methodology." ;
    ns1:subOrganizationWithin <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n765319> .

