    ns1:researchOverview "Much of my research focus is centered on providing diagnostic pathology services for a variety of conservation related projects. I currently provide support to special survival plans for African and Asian elephants, cotton-top tamarins, Key Largo woodrats, Guam Rails, Micronesian Kingfishers, and the migratory whooping crane project (Operation Migration, www.operationmigration.org)." .

