    ns1:researchOverview "Dr.  Oakland maintains an active and diverse research program. His interests  include: adaptive behavior and skills, their profiles for children with  various disabilities, and interventional strategies to help promote the  development of these behaviors and skills; children&rsquo;s temperament, its  impact on behavior, temperament-based values and learning styles, and  its development in other countries (currently with data from 14  countries); international issues important to psychology, including  school psychology; legal and professional issues important to the  practice of psychology; and test development and use. <strong><br /></strong>" .

