    ns1:overview "Professor Tucker teaches graduate courses in Financial Accounting and Accounting Theory at the Fisher School of Accounting. Dr. Tucker has presented her work 25 times in invited seminars or referred national conferences. Her work has been discussed in The Wall Street Journal, Barron's, Forbes, The Economist, Dow Jones News Service, and Reuters, to name just some of the financial press outlets. Dr. Tucker appeared on CNBC to discuss her research and its implications for the financial markets. Her work has clearly had an impact beyond the reach of the scholarly journals.<br />" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jenny.tucker@warrington.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-0214" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Tucker has been exceptionally productive and successfully in her research activities. Since joining the faculty five years ago as a new Ph.D. graduate, Jenny Tucker has published three papers in The Accounting Review and two forthcoming papers in Contemporary Accounting Research and Review of Accounting Studies. These journals are recognized as the leading journals in the discipline (top five journals). Moreover, her research has attracted attention by scholars, accounting and finance professionals, and the financial press." .

