        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n974020866> ;
    ns1:overview "Jeffrey D. Needell received his Ph.D. in 1982 from Stanford University, his M.A. (Latin American and colonial African history) in 1977 from Yale University, and his A.B. (history) in 1974 from the University of California at Berkeley. He joined the Department of History in 1987 after teaching at the University of Oregon (1982-85) and serving as an administrator (1985-87) in the Latin American Program of the Woodrow Wilson International Center for Scholars (Washington, D.C.). He has held fellowships from Fulbright-Hays, the Social Science Research Council, the National Endowment for the Humanities, and the American Philosophical Society, and has published a dozen articles." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jneedell@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-8328" .

