    ns1:overview "I am currently a Professor in the Department of Astronomy at the  University of Florida.  I received my BS in Physics from Yale University  in 1983 and my PhD in Astronomy from the University of Texas in 1990. I  spent 3.5 years as a postdoctoral researcher at the Harvard-Smithsonian  Center for Astrophysics and then 3 more years as a Hubble Fellow at the  University of Maryland. I joined the faculty at the University of  Florida in the fall of 1996. I received an NSF CAREER award in 1998 and a  Presidential Early Career Award for Scientists and Engineers in 1999." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "elada@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-1862" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My research is focused on understanding the origin, properties,  evolution and fate of young embedded clusters within molecular clouds." .

