    ns1:overview "In summary, one overall goal of Dr. Conrad has been to advance understanding of the mechanisms underlying maternal renal and cardiovascular adaptations to normal pregnancy. Another is to harness the &ldquo;lessons learned from normal pregnancy&rdquo; to facilitate the investigation of preeclampsia in which abnormal vasoconstriction and arterial stiffness pertain. A final aim is to see the fruits of this research through to the &ldquo;bedside&rdquo;. Thus, consultation and collaboration on investigations of relaxin as a potential therapeutic modality in preeclampsia, as well as in various cardiovascular diseases such as acute heart failure in the non-pregnant population is another major objective (and ones currently underway)." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "kpconrad@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-3791" .

