    ns1:overview "Shelley Trimble, PT is a Clinical Lecturer in the department of Physical        Therapy. She has over 25 years experience working with the pediatric population        in a variety of settings across the country. Ms. Trimble has been employed        at UF as adjunct faculty since 1995, working as a clinician with Children's        Medical Services, and providing guest lecturing and assistance in the pediatric        course. She previously participated in provision of clinical education training        through a series of professional and paraprofessional workshops provided        by Indiana University Institute for the Study of Developmental Disabilities,        and has several published clinical articles related to pediatric practice.        She has also had the honor of participating as a co-presenter at the annual        conference for the National Association for the Education of Young Children." .

