        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n885565187>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n970684431>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n988741766> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Parker is the program director of the neonatal nurse  practitioner program where she is involved in clinical and didactic  teaching of MSN students. She is board certified as a neonatal nurse practitioner by  the National Certification Corporation and has practiced as a neonatal  nurse practitioner for 21 years." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "parkela@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6384" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "<strong></strong>Dr. Parker's research involves the  benefits of breast milk in premature and critically ill infants.  She is  currently involved in research to increase the milk supply of mothers  of very premature infants" .

