        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n216266095>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n268026331>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n329995539>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n419577060>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n597841797>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n865421288>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n894353116>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n923747470>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n942570084>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n971724430> ;
    ns1:overview "Duke Cornell joined the advertising department after 10 years as a copywriter and creative supervisor at Long Haymes Carr and Lintas, working on such major accounts as Hanes, Planters,Lifesaver, Jefferson-Pilot Insurance, Rich Foods, Wachovia Bank, and Tyson and Holly Farms. She has won numerous industry awards, including &ldquo;Best of Show&rdquo; Addys for print and television, as well as recognition by the New York Art Director&rsquo;s Club and the International Film and Television Festival." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "lduke@jou.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-0447" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Duke-Cornell&rsquo;s gender work has addressed the links between identity, meaning making, and text as a consumption object. Advertising for fashion/beauty products, such as those featured in teen magazines, have been surprisingly consistent in the ways in the ways they portray girls and women. Therefore, as a teacher of creative, Dr. Duke-Cornell turned her attention to the ways in such &ldquo;creative&rdquo; concepts are produced with such uniformity and regularity. In an overview of the state of advertising research, Stewart (1992) noted, &ldquo;The topic of creativity is a surprisingly rare focus of research in a discipline that promotes creativity as one of its more important products&rdquo; (p. 13). The creative product &ndash; how it is conceived and developed &ndash; has been the focus of her recent research efforts. Not only is creativity an area that is under-studied, it meshes well with Dr. Duke-Cornell&rsquo;s interests, talents and teaching area.<br />" .

