    ns1:overview "Richard Burt received his BA and PhD from the University of California at Berkeley in 1977 and 1984, respectively. After holding a post-doctoral fellowship at the Medieval and Renaissance Center at Arizona State from 1984&ndash;86, Burt taught in the English Department at the University of Massachusetts, Amherst from 1986&ndash;2003. His dissertation on Shakespeare&rsquo;s comic form, gender, and scapegoating was directed by Professor Stephen Greenblatt, now at Harvard University." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "burt@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-2824" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Shakespeare, Renaissance drama, literary theory, film adaptation, the  Middle Ages in film and media, the erotics of pedagogy, telepolitics,  cinematic paratexts, and censorship" .

