    ns1:overview "<p>Dr. Horgas teaches research to undergraduate and graduate students and theory to PhD students. She is a fellow of the American Academy of  Nursing, the Gerontological Society of America, and a member of the  Florida Nurses Association and the Southern Nursing Research Society.  She has been the recipient of the Southern Nursing Research Society  Hartford Institute Geriatric Nursing Award, Springer Award for  Geriatric/Gerontological Nursing, the Harriet H. Werley New Investigator  Award, Midwest Nursing Research Society, and the Nightingale Award for  Excellence in Nursing Research.</p>" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "ahorgas@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-7622" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Horgas conducts research on aging, with a focus on  pain management in persons with dementia. She completed a Post Doctoral  Fellowship in Psychological Gerontology at the Free University of  Berlin. She is currently funded by the National Institute on Aging to  study cognitive interventions for older adults, and recently completed  an NINR-funded study of pain assessment in nursing home residents." .

