        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n743492805>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n749808205>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n839273522>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n883760854>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n920215897>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n992468511> ;
    ns1:overview "Before coming to the University of Florida, Dr. Figueroa-Haas practiced in Miami-Dade, Florida  as an Adult Care Nurse Practitioner specializing in cardiology, family  care, cosmetic surgery, and home health. As an Adult Health Nurse  Practitioner, she is Nationally Board Certified by the American Nurses  Credentialing Center (ANCC). Dr Figueroa-Haas currently teaches didactic  and clinical courses associated with the medical-surgical and critical  care adult client for graduate and undergraduate students. Additionally,  she advises the Doctoral of Nursing Practice (DNP) students &amp; is  the Track Coordinator for the Adult Health Practitioner Track." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "CindiFigueroa@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6424" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Figueroa-Haas&rsquo; research interest is namely centered  on psychological factors associated with women&rsquo;s health. Dr. Haas&rsquo; other  research interest concerns are on the psychological and social factors  that affect specific illnesses or client populations such as clients who  seek elective cosmetic surgery or the post menopausal client. Research  has been conducted to explore attitudes of specific populations  associated with clients who seek elective cosmetic surgery. In addition,  indebt analysis has been conducted on research findings which implied  association with increased suicide rates and women who had breast  implants. Currently, women&rsquo;s sexuality level in the postmenopasal client  is being explored." .

