    ns1:overview "The Department of Animal Sciences at the University of Florida has programs in genetics, management, meat science, molecular biology and physiology, and nutrition. My extension program is primarily based on my research interests. I coordinate and co-teach ANS 3251 \"Biology and management of dairy cattle\" and ANS 3250L \"Dairy Cattle Practicum\" in the&nbsp; Spring semester.<br />" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "devries@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-5594 ext. 227" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My research interests are in quantitative dairy systems management, including optimization of cow insemination, culling and replacement strategies under herd constraints, economics of reproductive strategies, productive life, animal health economics, statistical process control, and business analysis. I am interested in both methodological and applied aspects. The research activities are part of Multi-state Programs NC-1042 and S-104." .

