    ns1:overview "Dr. Martinez's has extensive experience in media relations and campaign design, implementation and evaluation. He has provided public relations services such as media relations and research in the United States, Latin America and the Middle East. Additionally, Mr. Martinez has coordinated and overseen public opinion and public relations research internationally. Mr. Martinez is a New York State certified Spanish language translator and interpreter.&nbsp; He has also performed research and professional work in English, Spanish and Brazilian Portuguese. He is co-founder and co-owner of Latin &amp; Hispanic Strategic Communications a communication consultancy firm as well as President &amp; CEO of BAM M&uacute;sica, Inc. an organizations promoting the arts and ethnic identity among all races." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "bmartinez@jou.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 846-2399" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "His current research interests include political communication, entertainment public relations, communication for development, and public relations targeting minorities in the United States. He has presented papers to the International Communication Association, the Association for Education in Journalism and Mass Communication, the National Communication Association and the New York State Communication Association. Dr. Martinez is also a an international speaker on issues of race, ethnicity, communications and development througout Latin America and in Europe. His teaching areas include communication theory, public relations writing, public relations research, public relations strategy, campaigns, international and ethnic public relations as well as visual communication." .

