    ns1:primaryEmail "tsbrophy@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-4476" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My research focuses on developing valid, reliable assessments in the arts, both at the classroom level and in large-scale settings. In Florida, I lead the Florida Music Assessment Task Force, which has developed a three-phase plan for music and art assessment in Florida public schools. The Phase I Elementary Music test was administered to 4th graders in 2007 (N = 9,473), and an online middle school and high school music test was developed and piloted in 2008. My research in the development of musical creativity has focused on the development of children&rsquo;s musical improvisations, and in 2010 I will complete a longitudinal, 10-year study of the melodic improvisations of a group of children. The study began when they were 7-years-old, and will conclude when they are 17-years-old.<br />" .

