        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n851241921>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n857818377>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n93667623>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n946708304> ;
    ns1:overview "My professional mission is to construct        a meaningful career dedicated to the patient, the student, and the science        of movement. Through the combined roles of clinical practitioner, physical        therapy teacher, and clinical researcher I am committed to an integrated        approach that will serve the individual, and society. My overall career        goal as a Clinical Assistant Professor in the PT program at UF is to inspire        my students to be dedicated to improving the quality of life of those they        treat through evidence-based practice, applied scientific inquiry, and community        outreach. My overall clinical research goal is to investigate mobility constraints        and potential intervention strategies in individuals with movement limitations.        More specifically, my objectives are to explore: 1) the postural control        requirements of mobility tasks, and 2) the specificity and intensity of        training essential for the restoration of the co-requisite postural control        elements of a task. Finally, I hope to continue to refine and improve upon        my clinical practice while pursuing the answers to those clinical questions." .

