        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n981838298> ;
    ns1:overview "Joao (Joe) Vendramini, Forage Specialist, has been closely involved with animal production and worked as farm manager in several large-scale beef cattle operations in Southern Brazil, that collectively maintained more than 10,000 beef cattle, 2,400 acres of sugarcane, and 1,200 acres of soybean and corn." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jv@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(863) 735-1314 ext. 205" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "His research program at IFAS UF Range Cattle REC at Ona will primarily focus on different aspects of the plant-animal interface in grazing systems and the effects of supplementation on forage utilization and animal performance. Joe will also investigate the most effective forage based animal production systems for Florida&rsquo;s cattle producers and the benefits of properly managed forage systems for the environment." .

