    ns1:outreachOverview "Chair, Litigation Committee of The Everglades Foundation, 2005-present<br /><br />Chair, Florida Supreme Court Committee on Privacy and Court Records, 2003-2005<br /><br />Member, Florida Constitution Revision (Chair of Style and Drafting Committee and selected Most Valuable Member), 1996-1998<br /><br />Speaker of the Florida House of Representatives, 1987-1988<br /><br />Member of the Florida House of Representatives, 1978-1988, served as House Majority Leader, 1985-1986<br /><br />Chair, Natural Resources Committee, 1984-1985<br /><br />" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "mills@law.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-0835" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Rapporteur, The American Bar Association Task Force on the Preservation of the Justice System, 2010<br /><br />Member, Advisory Commission to the World Justice Project (American Bar Association), 2007-08<br /><br />Rapporteur for the World Justice Project of the American Bar Association at the Buenos Aires Forum, Nov. 2007.<br /><br />Discussion Leader, Oxford Round Table on the Influence of Sir William Blackstone on American Education at Pembroke College Univ. Of Oxford, United Kingdom, August 6-11, 2006<br /><br />Presentation on The Evolution of Citizenship and Identity in the Global Community, at Utrecht University, 2002<br /><br />Speaker the Nineteenth International Symposium on Economic Crime, Jesus College, University of Cambridge, 2001<br /><br />Presentation on The Future of Governmental Ethics: Law and Morality, at Seventeenth International Symposium on Economic Crime, Jesus College, University of Cambridge, 1999<br /><br />Lecturer of two week course in Constitutional Law as part of the American Law Studies Program at the University of Warsaw, Poland, November 1999<br /><br />Instructor for Judges and Prosecutors Training 1997, Brazil and 2001 Gainesville<br /><br />Principal Investigator, Haiti Conflict Resolution Program 1996, under grant from United States Information Agency, E/P-96-36<br /><br />Editor, Polish Legal Database, on-line computerization of Polish laws and treaties, under contract with West Publishing Company, 1991-92<br /><br />" .

