        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n875815157> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Rosenberg&rsquo;s academic and clinical focus is on quality and patient safety. &nbsp;He is Physician Director for Quality and Safety for the Department of Medicine and leads the College of Medicine&rsquo;s Quality and Patient Safety Curriculum. &nbsp;He is a member of the ShandsUF Board Quality Committee. &nbsp;He continues to develop interprofessional protocols to standardize and improve quality of inpatient care for the treatment of patients. &nbsp;He has collaborated with health sciences center faculty on studies of medication errors of omission, causes of hyper and hypoglycemia, validity of automated alert systems to detect inappropriate prescribing of non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs in patients with renal insufficiency and development of patient safety curricula. &nbsp;He completed a collaborative research effort with 15 colleagues at multiple institutions focused on ways to improve the quality of pain management for primary care patients. &nbsp;He further serves as Associate Director of the College of Medicine&rsquo;s Comprehensive Assessment Services for Healthcare Practitioners and Competency Evaluation Program (&ldquo;Florida CARES&rdquo;). &nbsp; He directs the Department of Medicine&rsquo;s Annual Topics in Internal Medicine CME course and is regularly invited to provide instruction on patient safety, quality improvement, and preoperative assessment for CME audiences." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "eir@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 265-0651" .

