    ns1:overview "Howard Louthan is an Associate Professor of History and an affiliate faculty member in Religion at the University of Florida. He specializes in the history of early modern central Europe with an emphasis on cultural and religious history.Dr. Louthan teaches courses on early modern European history including undergraduate overviews of the Reformation and Renaissance periods, and the history of Christianity. He also leads graduate seminars on historiography, the Reformation and more specialized courses on the cultural and intellectual history of early modern Europe.<br />&nbsp;" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "louthan@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-3381" .

