    ns1:overview "Assistant Professor Matthew Jacobs received his Ph.D. in 2002 in U.S. History with a specialty in Foreign Relations from the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, his M.A. in 1996 from the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, and his B.A. in 1993 from Cornell University. He joined the University of Florida Department of History as Assistant Professor in 2003 after teaching as an adjunct for the Department for two years. He teaches undergraduate and graduate courses on twentieth century U.S. foreign relations, particularly with the Middle East, and international and world history more broadly. He has received the Department of History's John K. Mahon Award for Excellence in Undergraduate Teaching (2004-2005) and the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences Teacher of the Year Award (2009-2010)." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "mjacobs@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-3371" .

