        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n975075777> ;
    ns1:overview "Dr. Haddix is a graduate of the University of Florida where he received  his D.M.D. degree in 1977.  After six years of private practice in North  Carolina he joined the University of Florida Department of Endodontics  faculty in 1984, and is currently the Director of Pre-doctoral  Endodontics. He also is the Director of the Comprehensive Dentistry  Continuing Education program for those seeking Mastership in the Academy  of General Dentistry. He is a member of several professional  organizations, including the American Dental Association, the American  Association of Endodontists, the Academy of General Dentistry, Omicron  Kappa Upsilon, and is a Fellow of the American College of Dentists.  He  is also a past National President for Psi Omega Dental Fraternity." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jhaddix@dental.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-8482" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Haddix is currently involved in research involving gutta-percha obturation  techniques, nickel-titanium instrumentation, and restoring  endodontically treated teeth." .

