    ns1:overview "An associate dean and longtime professor of materials science and engineering who earned her doctorate from Stanford University is the University of Florida College of Engineering's first female dean. &ldquo;It&rsquo;s not really about me. It&rsquo;s a sign of where engineering has to go in the future,&rdquo; she said. &ldquo;We have to change the way engineering is perceived and we have to change the way it is introduced to potential students. This is especially important because engineering &mdash; and educating the next generation of engineers &mdash; is so critical to our country today.&rdquo; Abernathy, who specializes in the fabrication of semiconductor materials and devices, joined UF as a professor of materials science and engineering in 1993." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "caber@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-6000" .

