    ns1:overview "Julie E. Dodd is a professor in the Journalism Department. She teaches Writing for Mass Communication (MMC 2100) and Mass Communication Teaching (MMC 6930). She serves on the boards of the Journalism Education Association and Quill and Scroll International. She is co-chair of the JEA Mentoring Committee, which coordinates a program to match experienced media teachers with new high school media advisers. She has served as head and vice-head of the AEJMC Scholastic Journalism Division." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jdodd@jou.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-0452" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Dodd&rsquo;s research interests are uses of and effectiveness of technology in the media and in teaching and learning. She is interested in studying media representation of gender and race in sports coverage, media coverage of health and fitness issues, and scholastic journalism." .

