    ns1:overview "Professor Asares research, which focuses on understanding and improving auditors' decisions, has appeared in the leading accounting and psychology journals, and has been funded by the AICPA and KPMG Peat Marwick Research foundation. He is the current editor of the Journal of Accounting Literature. He is also interested in improving governance in transitional democracies. His monograph on the use of criminal law to uphold the Fiduciary Role of Public Officers has been published by the Ghana Center for Democratic Development." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "kwaku@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-8893" ;
