    ns1:researchOverview "Nearly all of my fieldwork has been conducted in the community of Ulukhaktok (formerly Holman) in the NWT of Canada.&nbsp; Ulukhaktok is a small community of roughly 420 people who identify themselves as Inuvialuit.&nbsp; I have done fieldwork there since 1992.Current research focuses on the intersection of the subsistence and wage economies in the Canadian Arctic, funded by the National Science Foundation, with George Wenzel of McGill University. Working in Ulukhaktok (Collings) and Clyde River, NU (Wenzel), we are interested in both (1) identifying the factors that influence individual participation in the Inuit subsistence system, and (2) documenting the degree to which the expansion of the wage sector of the economy over the past decade has modified or enhanced the material and social relations of Inuit subsistence systems." .

<http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n459587841> a ns2:Course,
        ns8:Thing .

