    ns1:overview "Donald Ault (PhD, 1968, University of Chicago) taught at the University of California, Berkeley, and at Vanderbilt University before coming to Florida in 1988. In 1972&ndash;74 he initiated curriculum changes at Berkeley by creating English 176 (&ldquo;Literature and Popular Culture&rdquo;) and English 177 (&ldquo;Literature and Philosophy&rdquo;). He teaches courses in Romanticism, in comics, animation, and movie serials, in literary theory, in William Blake, and in literature and science." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "ault@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-2854" .

