    ns1:overview "The Microbiology and Cell Science Department and it's Chair, Eric Triplett, are uniquely qualified to conduct the work proposed in this NIH Pathfinder Award proposal. We are a very diverse and inclusive faculty that nearly matches the diversity of underrepresented minorities in the state of Florida. Our diverse faculty members will be excellent role models for students at a diverse, urban community college. Our department has led successful, NSF-funded educational programs including a Research Experiences for Undergraduates program and two Course, Curriculum, and Laboratory Improvement (CCLI) grants. Prof. Triplett led both CCLI efforts. Prof. Triplett also led the effort to establish a distance education program to deliver his department's undergraduate curriculum to students over 330 miles away in Miami-Dade County. As a science discipline, this also requires on-site delivery of our laboratory courses. Prof. Triplett visits Miami Dade College monthly to recruit students and work with that College's administration." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "ewt@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-5430" .

