        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n94906443> ;
    ns1:overview "Matthew B. Walker, Ph.D. began his appointment at the University of  Florida in the Department of Tourism, Recreation and Sport Management in  the fall of 2008. Prior to joining UF, Dr. Walker was an assistant  professor at East Carolina University in the college of Health and Human  Performance. Dr. Walker teaches undergraduate and graduate courses in  finance, ethics, and research methods." ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Walker's research interests lie (generally) in business strategy but  with particular emphasis on business ethics and corporate social  responsibility. He has presented his research at several academic  conferences and his published manuscripts have appeared in a number of  academic outlets." .

