        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n944581470> ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Darby  Delane maintains an eclectic research agenda, but one that is anchored  by a solid commitment to investigating educational problems related to  equity and democracy in ways that promote social justice for students,  their teachers, and principals in public schools.&nbsp; As a qualitative  researcher she has most recently become interested in methods associated  with Participatory Action Research, as she believes that researchers  should work to both understand social phenomena and facilitate positive  change in society.&nbsp; Currently she is involved in research projects  seeking to (1) define and cultivate exemplary middle school leadership  and practices, (2) reveal and facilitate the power of Professional  Development School partnerships to impact student, teacher, prospective  teacher, and university faculty learning, and (3) name and disrupt  institutional narratives that support the &ldquo;struggling student&rdquo; identity,  as well as the implications that these constructions have on the life  chances of children, adolescents, and adults." .

