    ns1:overview """<p>Currently serving as a member of the Nanoscience Institute for Medical and Engineering Technologies (NIMET) and as a member of the HHMI Distinguished Mentor Selection Committee. Served as a member of the University Senate for one year and University Patent Committee for three years. As a Patent Committee member suggested to the Patent and Licensing Office methodologies to assist the faculty in patenting their novel ideas, and to streamline the overall patenting process at the University.</p>\r
Also serving as Director of the Particle Engineering Research Center at the University of Florida (NSF sponsored: 1994&ndash;05) with overall responsibilities of the research and education mission of the Center along with the fiscal management. This highly cross-disciplinary Center involves 20 faculty members, 30 graduate students, and more than 50 undergraduates from 10 different departments in five colleges across the campus. Forty companies are members of the Industrial Partners Program of the Center and actively participate in the research, education and technology transfer goals of the PERC.<br />\r
<p>&nbsp;</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "bmoudgil@perc.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 846-1194" .

