    ns1:researchOverview "I&nbsp;am an animal behaviorist interested in the evolution of alternative strategies and tactics and the economics and&nbsp;mechanisms of decision making. In particular, I am studying the evolution of mating and nesting behavior of horseshoe crabs. My current focus is on the evolution of multiple mating in female and group spawning by male horseshoe crabs. I am also interested in sexual selection, mate choice, and paternal care, the evolution of sex ratios, the evolution of life-history patterns (e.g. emergence and diapause) and the evolution of social behavior (e.g. nesting behavior of solitary and social wasps)." .

