    ns1:overview """<p><strong>Professional Focus</strong></p>\r
<p><i>One World: One Health</i></p>\r
<p>Control and Prevention of Emerging and Foreign Animal Diseases including those of Zoonotic Importance through Research, Education, Policy Development, and Emergency Response</p>\r
<p><strong>Field and Laboratory Experience of Emerging and Foreign Animal Diseases</strong></p>\r
<p>Foot-and-mouth disease; bluetongue; epizootic hemorrhagic disease of deer; rinderpest; peste des petits ruminants, cowpox, sheep and goat pox; lumpyskin disease; equine encephalitides (eastern, Venezuelan, West Nile); African swine fever; swine vesicular disease; pseudorabies; bovine herpes mammillitis, canine, equine, and avian influenzas.</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "pgibbs@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-4182" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Current Research Interests: Epidemiology and control of emerging viral diseases and their relationship to human and wildlife populations" .

