    ns1:overview "Dr. Bluck's theoretical and empirical work has appeared in such journals as Psychology and Aging, The Gerontologist, The Journal of Personality and Social Psychology,&nbsp; and Psychological Bulletin. She is a Fellow of the Gerontological Society of America, and a member of APA (Divisions 1, 20), the Society for Applied Research in Memory and Cognition, and the Society for Personology. Dr. Bluck is Associate Editor of Applied Cognitive Psychology, and on the editorial board of JPSP: PPID." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "bluck@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-3813" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Bluck's research concerns social cognition across the lifespan with a focus on how and why people remember the events of their own lives." .

