        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n978832052> ;
    ns1:overview "Michael M. Miyamoto serves as an Associate Chair and is a Professor in the Department of Zoology at the University of Florida. Dr. Miyamoto serves as a Member of Advisory Board of CLC bio A/S. He also serves on the Executive Committee for the UF Genetics Institute at the University of Florida. He teaches in the International Summer Workshop on Molecular Evolution at the Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole, Massachusetts. His research is in the areas of molecular ... evolution, molecular phylogenetics, population genetics, and bioinformatics. His work combines both empirical and theoretical approaches to the comparative analysis of macromolecular sequences and other genetic/genomic data. He has published over 70 articles in these fields, including recent publications on the application of hidden Markov models in sequence alignment and coalescence theory in population genetics analyses. Dr. Miyamoto has a Ph.D. in the Biological Sciences with an emphasis in Ecology and Evolution." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "miyamoto@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-3275" .

