    ns1:overview "Tace Hedrick received her BA in English and Writing from the University of Colorado at Denver and her MA and PhD in Comparative Literature (20th-century Latin-American and French Literature and Contemporary Theory) from the University of Iowa. Before her joint appointment between English and Women&rsquo;s Studies at the University of Florida, she taught at Pennsylvania State University, Harrisburg. She currently offers courses in Chicana/o and Latina/o literature and theory as well as in Women&rsquo;s Studies and feminist theory." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "tace@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-0390" .

