        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n97505191> ;
    ns1:overview "Professor Meneely joined the department in 2006 from Cornell University where he worked as a Research Associate in the department of Design and Environmental Analysis. Meneely&rsquo;s research examines strategies for enhancing creative performance in individuals, teams, and organizations. At the individual level, his research emphasizes cognitive awareness and thinking strategies to promote effective creative problem solving behavior. At the organizational level, Meneely&rsquo;s work examines design strategies for enhancing creative performance in the workplace through environmental, cultural, and procedural interventions. Meneely also examines the use of technology to support creative problem solving and is leading an effort to integrate digital sketching in design education. Meneely&rsquo;s work has been published in the Creativity Research Journal, the Journal of Interior Design, and has received awards at international conferences. He also serves as a reviewer for the Journal of Interior Design." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jmeneely@dcp.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-1436" .

