    ns1:overview "My research program explores the basic molecular mechanisms underlying fungal pathogenesis and fungal development. These investigations are largely focused on the broad host range phytopathogenic fungus Sclerotinia sclerotiorum. My teaching program includes the active mentoring of Graduate Students, teaching PLP 6905: Host Parasite Interactions I, and participation in the departmental core curriculum." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "rollinsj@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-4620" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My research focuses on studies of the broad host range plant pathogen Sclerotinia sclerotiorum and the identification and manipulation of molecular factors required for pathogenesis and development." .

