        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n993046110> ;
    ns1:overview "<strong>I am interested in multiple aspects of human evolution including population history and human adaptation. My lab analyzes human genomic variation that is neutral (in order to reconstruct human population history) and variation that is subject to natural selection (to study the origin and spread of human disease and human pathogens).</strong><strong> </strong><strong>We also use ancient DNA to reconstruct human population history. </strong><strong>For disease studies, we focus on candidate genes as well as genomic variation. We study populations from around the world with an emphasis on the Arabian Peninsula, Horn of Africa, New World, and East Asia for population history studies and the continental US, Puerto Rico, and the Democratic Republic of Congo for disease studies.</strong>" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "cmulligan@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-8092" .

