        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n999279702> ;
    ns1:overview """<p>Michael G. Perri, Ph.D., is dean at the University of Florida College of Public Health and Health Professions. Dr. Perri joined the UF faculty in 1990 as a professor of clinical and health psychology. At UF, Dr. Perri has held a variety of administrative positions, including head of the Health Psychology Division (1990&ndash;2004) and director of the Psychology Internship Program (1992&ndash;2004).&nbsp;From 2004 to 2007, he served as the college&rsquo;s associate dean for research.</p>\r
<p>Dr. Perri&rsquo;s research focuses on health promotion and disease prevention through changes in diet and physical activity. His current studies involve the development of effective programs for the management of obesity in underserved rural communities.&nbsp;Dr. Perri has contributed to 168 publications, including&nbsp;134 peer-reviewed journal articles,&nbsp;4 books, and&nbsp;30 book chapters/monographs. He has also co-authored papers published in the&nbsp;<em>New England Journal of Medicine, JAMA, Archives of Internal Medicine, Journal of Consulting and Clinical Psychology,&nbsp;</em>and&nbsp;<em>Health Psychology.</em></p>\r
<p>Dr. Perri&rsquo;s research has been supported through grants and contracts from the National Institutes of Health, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and private industry. Over the course of his career, he has been the principal investigator or co-investigator for more than $39 million in research grants and contracts.&nbsp;He is currently the principal investigator for $3.6 million in NIH grants and co-investigator for an additional $4.1 million in external awards.</p>\r
<p>The empirical findings from the 18 randomized controlled trials conducted by Dr. Perri&rsquo;s research team have had a significant impact on theory, research, and clinical care related to behavioral treatment of obesity.&nbsp;In 2008, Dr. Perri received the American Psychological Association&rsquo;s Samuel M. Turner Award for Distinguished Contributions to Applied Research in Clinical Psychology. In 2013, Dr. Perri received the Society of Behavioral Medicine&rsquo;s Distinguished Research Mentor Award.</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "mperri@phhp.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6214" .

