        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n9910901> ;
    ns1:overview "Angaran began his pharmacy career as a U.S. Air Force pharmacy  technician in 1962. He received his Bachelor of Science in Pharmacy from  Drake University, in 1968 and an Master of Science in Hospital Pharmacy  and Residency from the University of Wisconsin in 1970. As a critical  care clinical practitioner educator he served as pharmacy faculty at the  University of Wisconsin (1970-76), University of Minnesota (1976-1990)  and University of Florida (1990-95) where he was a Professor and Chair  of the Pharmacy Practice Department. He was elected to the ASHP board of  directors in 1988. Angaran left academia to pursue his interests in  delivery of pharmacy care at a distance, working for Medco Health  Solutions and a specialty pharmacy, Chronimed, Inc. In 1998, he  completed a one year ASHP managed care residency investigating  Telemedicine and Telepharmacy. In 2004, Angaran returned to the UF  College of Pharmacy in the Office of Experiential Programs. He became  the Medicare Part D point person for the UF College of Pharmacy and has  presented to health-care professionals and the public about the topic.  Most recently he was responsible for a $2.5 million contract to  establish a Medication Therapy Management call center in the College of  Pharmacy. Angaran has contributed to the pharmacy literature through  research publications, reviews and reflective writings about the life of  a clinical practitioner. He most recent award was the 2006 ASHP Award  for Distinguished Leadership in Health Systems Pharmacy." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "angaran@cop.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6231" .

