    ns1:overview "Margaret Portillo is the author of Color Planning for Interiors: An Integrative Approach to Color Wiley: 2009. The book presents an original criteria-based framework featuring process narratives by designers and clients. Portillo lead the FIDER Research council and currently serves on CIDA Standards committee. She chaired the Journal of Interior Design Publications Board and edited a special JID issue on narrative inquiry." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "mportill@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-0252" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Her research program focuses on design thinking and creativity, particularly emphasizing workplace environments. This psychologically-based research has furthered insights into optimizing creativity in design and across disciplines. The dissemination of her work has resulted in award winning presentations, articles, chapters and industry publications." .

