    ns1:overview "<p>The College of Engineering was established in 1910 under the leadership of its first dean, John R. Benton.&nbsp; It is the largest professional school, the second largest college and one of the three largest research units at the University of Florida.&nbsp; The curricula of the College of Engineering is planned to produce highly skilled engineers and provide each student with a broad range of degree and career choices.&nbsp; The College of Engineering fosters and provides world-class programs in engineering education, research and service to enhance the economic and social well-being of the citizens of Florida, the nation and the world.</p>" ;
    ns1:subOrganizationWithin <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n765319> .

