        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n972015439> ;
    ns1:overview "Butterweck is the current holder of Debbie and Sylvia DeSantis Term Professorship of Natural Products. She is the director of the Center for Drug Interaction Research and Education, joined the University of Florida&nbsp; in 2003 as the DeSantis Term Professorship in Natural Products. She established a research program in the area of pharmacodynamics and pharmacokinetics of herbal medications and natural products. Her goal is to establish a teaching program for pharmacists in the area of herbal medicines and natural products." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "butterwk@cop.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-7859" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Her research focuses on the development of new therapeutic concepts based on herbal medicines. In particular her laboratory has emphasized herbal medicines for the treatment of anxiety, depression and diabetes. These strategies are being evaluated on their own as well as in conjunction with proven therapies. In addition, Dr. Butterweck&rsquo;s research also emphazises the interaction between herbal medicines and conventional drugs (e.g. grapefruit juice drug-interactions).<br />" .

