    ns1:researchOverview "Mike Allen is a fisheries scientist whose research program  evaluates  fish population and fish community responses to changes in fishing   mortality, habitat, and species interactions.&nbsp; He and his students   evaluate the efficacy of various management strategies for improving and   sustaining fisheries.&nbsp;&nbsp; Allen approaches research using a combination   of empirical field studies, computer simulation modeling , and pond   experiments." .

