    ns1:researchOverview "My research interests focus  on curriculum development and evaluation issues in science and  environmental education; the cognitive, affective, and behavioral  impacts associated with learning science in informal settings; and the  role of global studies in the K-12 curriculum both in the United States  and overseas. I have engaged in curriculum and program development and  evaluation activities at the national and international level for  commercial textbook publishers, school districts, and numerous  governmental and non-governmental organizations. In addition, I have  conducted research science learning in informal settings and global  studies education in the U.S. and more than 20 countries throughout  Latin America, Africa, Asia, Europe, and the Caribbean." .

