    ns1:researchOverview "My research program addresses issues in plant ecology and restoration of ecosystem structure and function, including the establishment of native plant communities. Much of my work takes place in wetlands and aquatic habitats (wet meadows, marl prairies, riparian forests), but other interests include terrestrial ecosystems (Imperata cylindrica-invaded flatwoods) and cultural landscapes (roadsides, stormwater structures), such as roadsides. I also research the practice of ecological restoration, and the use of adaptive management as a way to improve land management.<br /><br />" .

