    ns1:overview "I'm a political anthropologist interested in culture, politics, and  political economy as they relate to forms of social inequality. My  approach is one that emphasizes race, gender, class, and (trans)national  identity as interlocking dimensions of difference, inequality, and  power. Over the years, I've done extensive ethnographic and documentary  research in the United States, Great Britain, and the Caribbean;  however, my research interests have taken me to other places as well,  including Mexico, Denmark, South Africa, and China." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "fayeharr@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-1020" .

