    ns1:overview "Dr. Muszynski has extensive experience in performing research on engineering materials and developing engineered solutions to material problems. He has over 20 years of experience in industry, academia and government, where he has developed material solutions to a wide variety of problems associated with the field. He has taught undergraduate and graduate courses in civil engineering and building construction while a visiting professor at the University of Florida in Gainesville. He has over 20 publications to his credit and holds 5 registered patents. <br />" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "larrym@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-1160" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Dr. Muszynski has expertise in physiochemical properties of materials; cement chemistry and concrete research; corrosion of steel in concrete, polymeric materials; materials testing and evaluation; failure analysis; fiber reinforced composite materials; and dynamic properties of materials." .

