    ns1:overview "Dr. Nealis teaches in the Family Nurse Practitioner  Program and the Pediatric Nurse Practitioner Program at the graduate  level. At the undergraduate level she teaches Child Health Nursing and  Professional Socialization Classes. She is the Clinical Track  Coordinator for the Pediatric Nurse Practitioner Program." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "nealirm@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6412" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "<strong></strong>Dr. Nealis&rsquo; research interests include  clinical outcome data and the integration of clinical genetics in the  undergraduate and graduate programs. Dr. Nealis&rsquo; dissertation work  focused on evaluating the effect of nonnutritive sucking on lingual  gastric lipase levels and fat absorption in preterm infants." .

