    ns1:overview """<p>Dr. Mary Ann Ferguson, chair of the University of Florida Faculty Senate, is a professor in the Public Relations Department of the College of Journalism and Communications. Since joining the UF faculty in 1982, Ferguson has served on numerous university committees and councils including two task forces on shared governance, the Faculty Welfare Council, the university's Institutional Review Board and the College of Medicine's Women Faculty Association. She chaired the UF Constitution Committee, the Faculty Educational Policy Group, and the Association of Academic Women.</p>\r
<p>In her college, she served as Associate Dean for Research, Director of the College's Communication Research Center, Affirmative Action Officer and chair of the College's Senate. Ferguson's research has received 41 contracts or grants totaling more than $1.37 million, including a three-year grant to evaluate the Florida anti-tobacco communication campaign. She has twice been designated as a Page Legacy Scholar by the Arthur W. Page Center at Pennsylvania State University for her research in corporate social responsibility.</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-6660" .

