    ns1:overview "My primary teaching responsibilities are the required and optional courses in digital architecture. In my six years of teaching at the University of Florida, I am the only School of Architecture faculty that has been able to teach these to our undergraduate and graduate students.These courses stem from years of continuing research into the evolving role of digital technology in the design process in both practice and academics. My secondary teaching responsibility is design studio.&nbsp; In my three years as an assistant professor, I have taught primarily upper level undergraduate design studios, but have also taught lower division studios.&nbsp; My design pedagogy fosters students&rsquo; own creative confidence through support of their ideas rather than my own, and focuses on the engagement of context both urban and natural, and the craft and detailing of architecture." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "maze@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-1476" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Since my knowledge base is grounded in this area of expertise, my research is focused on two critically adjacent areas: digital representation and visualization, and contemporary design issues and processes. My experience in architectural practice involved offices that have been pivotal in the evolution of digital technology in the architectural profession. As part of award winning design projects, we utilized state of the art modeling and rendering technologies that are still considered at the forefront and continue to influence the way young designers think about architecture. <br />" .

