    ns1:overview """<p>Epstein is a Assistant Professor in the Department of Pharmacotherapy  and Translational Research and Division of Internal Medicine at the  University of Florida. He earned his Doctor of Pharmacy from the  University of Florida in 2003. Subsequently, he completed an Internal  Medicine residency at the North Florida / South Georgia Veterans Health  System and returned to the University of Florida in 2004 where he  completed a Postdoctoral Fellowship in Family Medicine in the  Departments of Pharmacotherapy and Translational Research and Community  Health and Family Medicine.</p>\r
<p>Epstein is actively involved in teaching both in the College of  Pharmacy and the College of Medicine. His research interests include the  treatment and prevention of cardiovascular disease, and he is currently  the Primary Investigator for several ongoing studies in this field. He  serves as the Director of the Internal Medicine Pharmacotherapy Clinic  at the University of Florida where his practice interests include  hypertension, hyperlipidemia, diabetes, and anticoagulation. He lectures  nationally and internationally on these topics and has authored  articles published in New England Journal of Medicine, Drugs, American  Family Physician, Current Opinion on Investigational Drugs,  Pharmacotherapy, and Annals of Pharmacotherapy. Dr. Epstein serves as a  scientific reviewer for several Journals, including Emerging Infectious  Diseases, Annals of Internal Medicine, The Medical Letter, and Annals of  Pharmacotherapy and is on the Specialty Consultants Panel for both the  Pharmacist&rsquo;s Letter and Prescriber&rsquo;s Letter. He is an active member of  the American College of Clinical Pharmacy (ACCP) and the American  Society of Health System Pharmacists (ASHP). In 2005, Epstein was  recognized as a Board Certified Pharmacotherapy Specialist by ACCP.</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "epstein@cop.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6232" .

