        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n953786763>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n96721002>,
        <http://vivo.ufl.edu/individual/n971078240> ;
    ns1:overview """<p>In addition to being a professor, Gums&nbsp; holds the title of Director  of Clinical Research in Family Medicine. Gums joined the faculty at the  University of Florida in 1985. He is actively involved in teaching both  in the UF College of Pharmacy and the College of Medicine . He has  received Teacher of the Year award from the UF Department of Family  Medicine twice since joining the faculty.</p>\r
<p>He has authored over 75 peered-review articles, 14 continuing  education programs, 15 posters and abstracts, and 9 book chapters. He  has given over 100 presentations including national and internationally  invited presentations to pharmacy and medical associations. He maintains  an active clinical research program and is currently the principal  investigator of the ARM Program and an investigator on a NIH grant  investigating the pharmacogenetic determinants of antihypertensives.</p>\r
<p>In 1997, he received the Outstanding Clinical Practice Award from  ACCP. Most recently, Gums served as a Primary Health Care Policy Fellow  with the Secretary of Health and Human Services in Washington DC .</p>""" ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "jgums@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-8318" .

