    ns1:primaryEmail "walter.leite@coe.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-4302" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "My research interests are structural equation modeling  (SEM), statistical analysis of longitudinal data, scale construction and  validation, response bias, and method effects. SEM is an overarching  theme that influences all my other research interests. From the methods  for statistical analysis of longitudinal data, I am particularly  interested in latent growth modeling (LGM) and its extensions (second  order, multilevel, mixture, nonlinear and accelerated LGM). In the area  of scale construction and validation, I have developed a method of item  selection for short forms of scales based on the Ant Colony Optimization  Algorithm. In the area of response bias and method effects, I  investigated the dimensionality and reliability of the Marlowe Crowne  Social Desirability scale and Balanced Inventory of Desirable  Responding, which are commonly used scales to measure social  desirability bias. I am also interested in the use of mixture modeling  and multitrait-multimethod structural equation modeling for diagnosing  and controlling response bias and method effects." .

