    ns1:researchOverview "Research thus far has dealt with the measurement and understanding of in  situ rates of biogeochemical processes involving carbon, nitrogen,  phosphorus and sulfur cycling. Ecosystems of interest include both salt  and freshwater wetland marshes, lakes, rivers, and springs. A  combination of traditional nutrient and flux analyses, enzyme  activities, novel microscopic and isotopic approaches are utilized. More  recent studies have focused on measurement of cyanobacterial mat  nitrogenase activity, the use of stable isotopes (natural abundance and  enriched levels) to infer biogeochemical processes and trace the fate of  nutrients, and measurements of bacterial production and dissolved  organic matter interactions in aquatic systems. The ultimate goal of  this research is to better understand how environmental factors control  biogeochemical reactions in landscape settings. <br />" .

