    ns1:outreachOverview "I direct an NSF-funded GK-12 program called SPICE (Science Partners in Inquiry-based Collaborative Education).&nbsp; We pair graduate students with middle school teachers and train them to teach science in a way that will excite kids and turn them onto science.&nbsp; We do so through inquiry-based lessons that empower kids to become scientists, themselves.&nbsp; Science becomes exploratory rather than a collection of stale facts.&nbsp; Equally important, SPICE improves communication and partnership skills of graduate students, who we hope will remain active in outreach activities for the rest of their careers." ;
    ns1:overview "I am an evolutionary ecologist.&nbsp; My students and I study lots of topics, most related to tropical ecology and plant-animal interactions.&nbsp; I teach an Avian Biology course and direct SPICE (Science Partners in Inquiry-based Collaborative Education), a training program that places graduate students in disadvantaged middle schools." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "dlevey@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-9169" ;
    ns1:researchOverview """<p>The overarching theme of my research is the evolutionary ecology of plant-animal interactions.&nbsp;&nbsp; I&rsquo;m currently focusing on three topics:</p>\r
<ul>\r
<li><a href="http://people.biology.ufl.edu/dlevey/research-habitat.html">The effectiveness of habitat corridors in conservation and their impact on the spatial ecology </a></li>\r
<li><a href="http://people.biology.ufl.edu/dlevey/research-fruit-compounds.html">The function of secondary compounds in ripe fruits</a>, and</li>\r
<li><a href="http://people.biology.ufl.edu/dlevey/research-codependency.html">The importance of fruiting plants to birds and, likewise, of birds to fruiting plants</a>.&nbsp; </li>\r
</ul>\r
<p>I'm also interested in migratory birds, especially those in Central and South America:</p>\r
<ul>\r
<li><a href="http://people.biology.ufl.edu/dlevey/research-migratory-birds.html">Evolutionary ecology of migratory birds</a></li>\r
</ul>\r
<p><br /> And, I dabble in other areas:</p>\r
<ul>\r
<li><a href="http://people.biology.ufl.edu/dlevey/research-mockingbirds.html">Mockingbirds' ability to recognize individual humans</a></li>\r
<li><a href="http://people.biology.ufl.edu/dlevey/research-ant-ecology.html">Ant ecology</a></li>\r
<li><a href="http://people.biology.ufl.edu/dlevey/research-digestive-phys.html">Digestive physiology</a></li>\r
<li>And, even though my teenage daughters disown me when they hear me claim&nbsp; this:&nbsp; <a href="http://people.biology.ufl.edu/dlevey/research-dung.html">Creative uses of dung</a></li>\r
</ul>""" .

