    ns1:primaryEmail "vcrecy@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 292-9416" ;
    ns1:researchOverview """<p>The main focus of Dr. de Crecy-Lagard's laboratory is to utilize the  power of microbial genetics to make efficient use of the avalanche of  genomic information now available. By combining comparative genomics  approaches with experimental verification, new enzymes, pathways and  chemistries that had previously evaded identification are revealed.</p>\r
<p>We have identified several new tRNA modification families  that are now under study. By using a new model organism, the naturally  transformable bacterium Acinetobacter ADP1, very simple protocols for  genetic manipulation have been developed and are now being used to test  predictions, build selection strains, and perform pathway engineering.  Finally, the use of experimental evolution protocols to adapt bacteria  to new metabolic constraints is being explored.</p>""" .

