    ns1:overview "Candy Carmel-Gilfilen is a LEED accredited professional, licensed interior designer in the state of Florida, and an NCIDQ certified interior designer that has practiced professionally in Ohio and Michigan. Professor Carmel-Gilfilen currently serves as the Interior Design Undergraduate Coordinator and directs the Design Field Experience Program." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "carmelcn@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 294-1431" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Her research centers on crime prevention and design security. She is currently involved in a study of novice and professional shoplifter&rsquo;s perceptions of retail environments. Candy&rsquo;s other research track focuses on pathways of student development and has been published in the Journal of Interior Design and Design Studies." .

