    ns1:primaryEmail "dawson@coe.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-4177" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "I study the ways in which  educational technologies impact teaching and learning in K-12 and post  secondary environments. Since 2006 much of my K-12 research has focused  on the impact of Title II-D Enhancing Education through Technology  (EETT) competitive funding on student achievement and teaching  practices. This research has involved nearly 1800 teachers in 298  schools within 33 Florida districts. In addition to reports published by  the Florida Department of Education, this work has appeared in the <em>Journal of Research on Technology in Education</em> and is currently accepted for publication in the <em>Journal of Educational Computing Research</em>.  In addition, this work was recognized with an Outstanding Paper Award  at the 2008 Society for Information Technology and Teacher Education  (SITE) conference and with an Outstanding Paper nomination at the  American Educational Research Association (AERA). <br />" .

