    ns1:researchOverview "Margaret James, Ph.D., investigates factors affecting the metabolism and toxicity of drugs and other xenobiotics in humans and animal species, including aquatic species. She was chosen as the Jack C Massey Professor of Pharmacy for 2006-2011, and as a University of Florida Research Foundation Professor, 1997-2000. Her laboratory studies mechanisms of uptake, biotransformation, excretion and toxicity of xenobiotics, especially environmental chemicals. James also is interested in the influence of xenobiotics on the metabolism of steroid hormones." .

