    ns1:overview "Bill is an assistant professor and wildlife extension specialist in the University of Florida's Department of Wildlife Ecology and Conservation with  over 12 years experience . His focus areas include wildlife ecology and  management and integrating wildlife management into agricultural  systems. Bill received his PhD in Wildlife Management from Texas Tech  University, his MS in Biology from Eastern Kentucky University, and BS  in Wildlife Management from the University of New Hampshire." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "docg@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 846-0575" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Using state-of-the-art research methodologies to understand biological and socio-economic aspects of wildlife and their management in real-world environments such as working ranches, I have developed an applied research program focused on integrating wildlife management and other land-uses, particularly agriculture." .

