    ns1:primaryEmail "lesollen@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-3420" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Studies are conducted assessing grassland ecology, management, and utilization. Areas of recent focus include nutrient cycling in grasslands, the role of grasslands in providing ecosystem services to society, and the use of grassland plants as bioenergy crops. Research has developed management practices that improve spatial distribution of nutrient return to grasslands by herbivores and has described the impact of grassland management on plant litter production and nutrient release. The societal benefits of grasslands in carbon sequestration, preservation of water quality, and improvement in soil quality have been described. Studies are underway evaluating the potential of a range of grasses for bioenergy uses and assessing alternatives to commercial fertilizers as nutrient sources for production of bioenergy crops." .

