    ns1:researchOverview "My research agenda is about multicultural counseling, group work, chaos theory, liberation psychology, technology, supervision, multicultural counseling, prisons, Puerto Rican studies, identity development, and gang-related behavior. Specifically, my primary research focuses is in complexity and how indigenous healing techniques are a necessary ingredient when working with ethnic minority populations in the United States. My additional research interests are in studying the implications of social injustice and oppression in counseling and psychotherapy with ethnic minorities, in particular, with school age Latinos/Latinas in the United States.&nbsp;" .

