    ns1:overview "I am an associate professor of psychology at the University of Florida investigateing memory and language processes in younger and older adults, specifically the processes involved in retrieving words and the changes in these processes that occur with normal aging." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "abrams@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 392-0601" ;
    ns1:researchOverview "Specific areas of interest include: (1) memory retrieval failures such as the tip-of-the-tongue states, which are naturally-occurring retrieval failures that are characterized by a temporary inability to recall a known word; and (2) language errors such as the production of spelling errors and homophone substitution errors." .

