    ns1:overview "Charles J. Kibert is a Professor and Director of the Powell Center for Construction and Environment at the University of Florida. He is co-founder and President of the Cross Creek Initiative, a non-profit industr /university joint venture seeking to implement sustainability principles into construction. He is co-chair of the Curriculum and Accreditation Committee of the U.S. Green Building Council and helped create the first ever student chapter of the USGBC for which he serves as faculty advisor." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "ckibert@ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-1189" .

