    ns1:overview "Hendeles is a Professor in the College of Pharmacy and also in the  Department of Pediatrics at the University of Florida. Among his current  research interests are the improvement of adherence to asthma  medications and delivery of inhaled drugs to young children. He is a  consultant to FDA&rsquo;s Pulmonary Division, and previously served on the  Coordinating Committee of NIH&rsquo;s Asthma Education Program, as well as  CDC&rsquo;s Expert Panel on Asthma Guidelines for Emergency Medical Services.  Hendeles provides advice on drug therapy and teaches in the Pediatric  Pulmonary Clinic at the University of Florida." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "hendeles@cop.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6027" .

