    ns1:overview "Doty graduated with his Doctor of Pharmacy degree from the University of  Tennessee in 1988. He finished a general clinical residency at the  Veterans Administration Medical Center in Memphis Tennessee in 1989. He  accepted an appointment in the Department of Pharmacy Practice in 1989  and was the Associate Director of the Computer Applications in Pharmacy  Center at the University of Florida until it closed in 1991. He is  currently a Clinical Associate Professor in the Department of  Pharmacotherapy and Translational Research as well as the Director of  Experiential Programs at the University of Florida College of Pharmacy.  He coordinates the four early experiential courses as well as developing  and scheduling all the senior student advanced practice experiences." ;
    ns1:primaryEmail "doty@cop.ufl.edu" ;
    ns1:primaryPhoneNumber "(352) 273-6228" .

